WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.014
The headline result is that DRAGONN cuts
compression time by up to seventy percent compared

00:00:06.094 --> 00:00:08.960
to the best existing sparsification methods.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.571
Reaching the same level of convergence,

00:00:11.651 --> 00:00:18.602
it delivers up to three-and-a-half times higher
total training throughput than Deep Gradient Compression,

00:00:18.682 --> 00:00:23.223
and up to nearly thirty-six times over full
gradient synchronization,

00:00:23.303 --> 00:00:27.307
all while matching the test accuracy of full
synchronization.

00:00:27.387 --> 00:00:31.660
Importantly, its advantage over DGC grows as more
GPUs are added,

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.870
which signals strong scalability,

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:38.490
and the authors expect the gains to widen further
on faster networks.
